# Dashboard API client usage

All server-side API calls in the client dashboard must go through `@shipshout/api-client` — not hand-built `fetch` URLs.

## Layering

| Layer | File pattern | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Transport | `@shipshout/api-client` (`ApiClient` + generated `ApiSdk`) | Cookie auth interceptor; `fetchProtected` (401 retry) / `fetchPublic` (one-shot) |
| Domain API | `*.api.ts` (`AuthApi`, `ShoutoutsApi`, …) | Thin wrappers around `ApiClient.fetchProtected` / `fetchPublic` |
| Server actions | `*.actions.ts` | Form validation, redirects, `revalidatePath`; delegate to matching `*.api.ts` |
| Errors | `api/api-error.utils.ts` (`ApiErrorUtils`) | Extract Nest-style error messages from hey-api results |

## Do

```typescript
import { ApiClient } from '@shipshout/api-client';

// authenticated
return ApiClient.fetchProtected((api) => api.publishShoutout({ path: { id: shoutoutId } }));

// public / auth endpoints (no 401 retry)
return ApiClient.fetchPublic((api) => api.authControllerLogin({ body, redirect: 'manual' }));
```

## Don't

- Call raw `fetch('/…')` when `ApiSdk` exposes the endpoint
- Spread `requestOptions` manually — the interceptor injects auth headers
- Put request/response mapping in `*.actions.ts` — keep actions thin
- Duplicate cookie/header building or 401 retry outside `ApiClient`
- Use `fetchProtected` for login/register/refresh — 401 is a real failure; refresh must not recurse
- Instantiate `ApiSdk` directly from pages/routes — go through domain `*.api.ts` methods

## Exceptions

- **Auth / public endpoints** — `ApiClient.fetchPublic` via `AuthApi`
- **Set-Cookie handling** — `AuthUtils.applyToCookieStore` / `applyToNextResponse` for login responses; `ApiClient.fetchProtected` applies refresh cookies itself
- **Login redirect** — `redirect: 'manual'` on `authControllerLogin` only
- **SSE streams** — domain API + `fetchProtected` with `parseAs: 'stream'`

## Regenerate client

```bash
bun run openapi:generate
```

Requires the API serving OpenAPI at `http://localhost:8000/docs/openapi.json`.
